-- title:
--   Properness over ℤ of the two-chart integral model
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $N \neq 0$ and let $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull N` be the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}$ inside the field of Laurent series $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the set of expansions $\{\,\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb{Q}\,d\ jq : d \neq 0,\ d \mid N\,\}$, and let $j =$ `jFull N` be the element of $F$ given by the $q$-expansion $jq$. Consider the two chart algebras of $F$ over $\mathbb{Z}$ attached by `chartAlg` to the singletons $\{j\}$ and $\{j^{-1}\}$, and the scheme [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel ℤ F j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) defined as the pushout, in schemes, of the two morphisms $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the inclusions of these two subalgebras into the subalgebra of $F$ serving as the overlap chart. The morphism [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.toBase ℤ F j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L258) to $\mathrm{Spec}\,\mathbb{Z}$ is the map obtained from the two structure morphisms $\mathrm{Spec}$ of $\mathbb{Z} \to \mathrm{chartAlgFin}$ and $\mathbb{Z} \to \mathrm{chartAlgInf}$ by the universal property of the pushout. The assertion is that this morphism is proper, in the sense of Mathlib's `IsProper`.
--
--   This is the properness of the integral model of the modular curve of level $N$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,\mathbb{Z}$, built here by glueing the two chart algebras of the modular function field along $j$ and $j^{-1}$; for $N$ prime it plays the role of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(p)$ over $\mathbb{Z}$. It is used in the construction and comparison of the Deligne–Rapoport model, in particular in the results on isomorphisms compatible with `toBase` and on closedness of residue points.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_IgusaScheme_isProper_toBase_int.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_IgusaScheme
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open AlgebraicGeometry ModularCurve ModularCurve.IgusaScheme
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option maxHeartbeats 800000

theorem ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.isProper_toBase_int (N : ℕ) [NeZero N] :
    IsProper (AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.toBase ℤ ↥(modularFunctionFieldFull N) (jFull N)) := by sorry
